# ============================================================================
# deploy/single/.env — the single-node profile's configuration.
#
#   Copy to `.env` (gitignored) and fill in. Everything the giftable install
#   needs is here; the installer writes this file, but it is plain enough to
#   fill by hand.
#
#   make-secrets.sh GENERATES the credentials that are missing (the LiteLLM
#   master/salt keys, the Postgres and Neo4j passwords, the n8n encryption
#   key) and writes them BACK into this file. Two of them must then never
#   change:
#     LITELLM_SALT_KEY    encrypts the stored LiteLLM virtual keys
#     N8N_ENCRYPTION_KEY  decrypts the stored Gmail OAuth credential
#   A restore under a different value leaves the rows present but
#   undecryptable. Back this file up somewhere OUTSIDE the install tree.
# ============================================================================

# ── The LLM provider ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NOT in this file (2026-08-30). Setup's `llm` phase creates the four required
# aliases (cc-default, graphiti-llm, cc-embedding, gpt-4.1-nano) as skeletons
# in LiteLLM's database and PAUSES so you enter the provider yourself in its
# UI — http://127.0.0.1:4000/ui — model ids, api_base, and the key (stored
# encrypted under LITELLM_SALT_KEY). Re-running `./setup.sh llm` validates
# every alias with a real request and continues. Two things to get right:
#   * api_base is what the CONTAINER dials: for a server on THIS machine use
#     http://host.containers.internal:<port>/v1, never 127.0.0.1/localhost
#     (bitten 2026-08-28, Windows). A remote endpoint uses its normal URL.
#   * a key the server ignores can be `none`, but the field must be non-empty.
# List what a server names its models with:
#   CC_LLM_BASE_URL=<url>/v1 CC_LLM_API_KEY=<key> ./discover-llm.sh models

# The embedding model's output dimension. LEAVE IT BLANK: the `llm` phase of
# setup.sh MEASURES it (embeds one string through the cc-embedding alias and
# counts the vector) and writes it here. Never assume it from a model card — a
# mis-sized vector does not error, it corrupts the Neo4j index. Effectively
# permanent: changing it later means dropping the index and re-embedding the
# whole graph, which is why setup.sh REFUSES to overwrite a different value
# that is already here.
CC_EMBED_DIM=

# NOTE for the APP's .env (the repo root one, not this file): the curation
# writer embeds through a LiteLLM ALIAS, not the upstream model name. On this
# profile set, in the app's .env:
#   CC_EMBED_ALIAS=cc-embedding
#   CC_EMBED_DIM=<same value as above>
# (App defaults are the homelab's qwen3-embedding-local/1024.)

# ── Names and ports ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Pod names are also DNS names on the podman network (kube play implements no
# Services), so this prefix travels into every cross-pod reference. Change it
# only to run a second, isolated stack on the same machine — and change the
# network and every port below with it.
CC_POD_PREFIX=cc-
CC_NETWORK=cc-single

# Loopback host ports. The defaults match what the app's .env already assumes.
CC_PG_PORT=5442
CC_LITELLM_PORT=4000
CC_LITELLM_DB_PORT=5443
CC_GRAPHITI_PORT=8000
CC_NEO4J_BOLT_PORT=7687
CC_NEO4J_HTTP_PORT=7474
CC_N8N_PORT=5678
CC_CRAWLER_PORT=8091

# ── What to install (setup.sh reads these; 1 = yes, 0 = no) ─────────────────
# n8n is only needed by an n8n-backed integration (today: Gmail). Off by
# default — skip it and the install is two containers lighter.
CC_ENABLE_N8N=0
# The crawl service (Chromium, rung 2 of docs ingestion). Its image is built
# locally and is large; rung 1 (plain HTTP fetch) still works without it.
CC_ENABLE_CRAWLER=1
# The agent sandbox. On this profile its backend is ROOTLESS PODMAN, not the
# k3s profile's gVisor — weaker isolation, stated plainly. The runner itself
# is a host process you start alongside the API (see README.md).
CC_ENABLE_SANDBOX=1
# No public package index reachable? 1 makes the app phase install from
# requirements.lock instead of resolving, and turns the pypi/npm reachability
# probes into information rather than warnings. See deploy/AIRGAP.md.
CC_AIRGAP=0

# Tag of the locally-built graphiti image (build-graphiti-image.sh).
CC_GRAPHITI_TAG=1.0.2-anthropic

# ── Where every dependency comes from ───────────────────────────────────────
# `setup.sh fetch` (the phase right after preflight) acquires EVERYTHING the
# install needs — images by digest from images.txt, the three locally-built
# images, the Python resolution, the cockpit's npm tree — before anything is
# deployed, and STOPS (exit 3) on the first artifact it cannot get, naming
# the seam below that governs it. Fix the mirror and re-run, or point that
# one artifact at a bundle. Nothing falls back on its own; the choice is
# written here so a re-run and an update make the same one.
#
# Mirrors: blank = the public source. Only HOSTS are variables; a mirror that
# re-namespaces image PATHS needs the path edited in images.txt + the
# templates — that is deployment-time reality no variable can express.
#CC_REGISTRY_DOCKERIO=docker.io
#CC_REGISTRY_GHCR=ghcr.io
#CC_REGISTRY_MCR=mcr.microsoft.com
# Debian mirror for the two image builds that apt-get (graphiti, sandbox).
# Build containers do not see the host's apt config, so this goes in as a
# build-arg and REWRITES /etc/apt/sources.list.d/debian.sources from the
# base image's /etc/os-release (deb822; the slim images ship no
# sources.list at all). The main archive and the security archive are
# separate paths on every Debian mirror; leave the second blank to build
# without the security suite (fine for reproducible pins, not for CVE
# currency).
#CC_APT_MIRROR=https://MIRROR_HOST/debian
#CC_APT_SECURITY_MIRROR=https://MIRROR_HOST/debian-security
# PyPI simple index. Exported as BOTH PIP_INDEX_URL and UV_DEFAULT_INDEX —
# uv reads no PIP_* variable and no pip.conf (and UV_INDEX_URL is deprecated).
#CC_PYPI_INDEX_URL=https://MIRROR_HOST/pypi/simple
# Where uv downloads a CPython build when the host has no 3.12
# (UV_PYTHON_INSTALL_MIRROR; a file:// directory works).
#CC_PYTHON_MIRROR=https://MIRROR_HOST/python-build-standalone
# npm registry, only needed when the cockpit is BUILT here (see
# CC_SOURCE_COCKPIT). Exported as NPM_CONFIG_REGISTRY. package-lock.json's
# resolved URLs point at registry.npmjs.org, which npm rewrites to this
# automatically (its `replace-registry-host` default).
#CC_NPM_REGISTRY=https://MIRROR_HOST/npm/
# Trust and proxy for HOST-SIDE acquisition (fetch/app: curl, uv/pip, npm).
# CC_CA_BUNDLE is the same fact as the root .env's CC_CA_BUNDLE (integration
# trust): a private CA the tools must trust — here for a TLS-intercepting
# proxy or a self-signed mirror. Fanned out by setup.sh to CURL_CA_BUNDLE,
# SSL_CERT_FILE (uv/openssl), REQUESTS_CA_BUNDLE, NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS and
# NPM_CONFIG_CAFILE. podman PULLS read the host trust store, not this — see
# deploy/AIRGAP.md. Never "fix" a cert failure by disabling verification.
#CC_CA_BUNDLE=/etc/ssl/certs/corp-root.pem
# Mandatory egress proxy, fanned out to http(s)_proxy in both cases, with
# no_proxy pinned to loopback (every phase curls 127.0.0.1). podman forwards
# the proxy variables into builds on its own; credentials belong in ~/.netrc,
# never in this file.
#CC_PROXY=http://proxy.corp.example:8080
#
# Per-artifact source: mirror (default — pull/build/resolve through the
# mirrors above, or the public sources) or bundle (import from CC_BUNDLE_DIR,
# produced on a connected machine by `./bundle.sh export`). A bundle is a
# snapshot of THIS release; mirrors keep serving future releases' pins.
#CC_BUNDLE_DIR=/media/usb/cc-bundle
#CC_SOURCE_IMAGES=mirror     # the pulled images in images.txt
#CC_SOURCE_GRAPHITI=mirror   # build-graphiti-image.sh (needs apt + PyPI)
#CC_SOURCE_SANDBOX=mirror    # build-sandbox-image.sh  (needs apt + npm)
#CC_SOURCE_CRAWLER=mirror    # build-crawler-image.sh  (needs PyPI only)
#CC_SOURCE_COCKPIT=mirror    # npm ci + build here     (needs node 22 + npm)
#CC_SOURCE_PYTHON=mirror     # requirements.lock from PyPI, or the wheelhouse

# ── Generated by make-secrets.sh if left blank — see the header ─────────────
LITELLM_MASTER_KEY=
LITELLM_SALT_KEY=
LITELLM_POSTGRES_PASSWORD=
NEO4J_PASSWORD=

# OPTIONAL, never generated — LiteLLM admin-UI login. Unset means the UI logs
# in as username `admin` with LITELLM_MASTER_KEY as the password.
#UI_USERNAME=
#UI_PASSWORD=

# Credentials Graphiti uses to reach LiteLLM. On a real install these should
# be LiteLLM VIRTUAL keys, each scoped to one model group, so a leak in one
# cannot spend through another. make-secrets.sh falls back to the master key
# when they are blank, which works but is coarser.
GRAPHITI_LLM_API_KEY=
EMBEDDER_API_KEY=
RERANKER_API_KEY=

# ── Only used when optional-n8n.yaml is played ──────────────────────────────
N8N_ENCRYPTION_KEY=
N8N_DB_USER=n8n
N8N_DB_PASSWORD=
N8N_DB_NAME=n8n
